<title>CHINA: China banks issue 75 bln yuan non-tradeable bonds.</title>
<headline>China banks issue 75 bln yuan non-tradeable bonds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's big five banks issued a total of 75.957 billion yuan ($9.15 billion) worth of tradeable bonds from 1 March to May 10, the Financial News said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>That was 61.75 percent of the target for the year of 123 billion yuan, it quoted the central bank as saying.</p>
<p>Of the total, 20.652 billion yuan were two-year bonds, 43.597 billion yuan were three-year bonds and 11.708 billion yuan were five-year bonds, it said.</p>
<p>($1.0 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
